<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title><%= h.call(title) %> · GHAS Me Up</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <div class="page">
    <a class="back" href="../">&larr; GHAS Me Up</a>
    <h1 style="color: <%= h.call(accent) %>"><%= h.call(title) %></h1>
    <div class="meta">
      <span>Ruby <%= h.call(ruby_version) %></span>
      <span>built <%= h.call(built_at) %></span>
      <span>stamp (md5) <%= h.call(BUILD_STAMP) %></span>
      <span>preview token <%= h.call(PREVIEW_TOKEN) %></span>
    </div>

    <%= content %>

    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Gem</th><th>Locked version</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <%- gems.each do |gem| -%>
        <tr><td><%= h.call(gem[:name]) %></td><td><%= h.call(gem[:version]) %></td></tr>
        <%- end -%>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <p class="note">Intentionally outdated. Source:
      <a href="<%= h.call(source_url) %>">ruby/</a>. See
      <strong>Security &rarr; Dependabot</strong> on GitHub.</p>

    <section class="security-demo" aria-labelledby="security-demo-title">
      <h2 id="security-demo-title">Security findings demo</h2>
      <p>These are advisory examples associated with pinned dependencies, not verified
        application vulnerabilities. Current alert status and severity must be checked in
        the repository's <a href="https://github.com/epabishai/ghas-me-up/security/dependabot">Dependabot alerts</a>.</p>
      <div class="demo-actions">
        <button type="button" data-show="before-ruby" aria-expanded="false">Show vulnerabilities / Before autofix</button>
        <button type="button" data-show="after-ruby" aria-expanded="false">After autofix</button>
        <button type="button" data-autofix>Run agentic autofix</button>
      </div>
      <div id="before-ruby" class="finding-view" hidden>
        <h3>Before autofix · Ruby</h3>
        <p>Illustrative dependency advisories; they do not establish reachability or exploitability.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2021-28834">kramdown 2.3.0 · CVE-2021-28834</a> — <code>ruby/Gemfile.lock</code></li>
          <li><a href="https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2020-8130">rake 12.3.2 · CVE-2020-8130</a> — <code>ruby/Gemfile.lock</code></li>
        </ul>
        <p>Severity and whether these alerts remain open are not available in this static page.
          No source-code finding or affected runtime behavior has been verified. Manual triage
          in GitHub is required.</p>
      </div>
      <div id="after-ruby" class="finding-view" hidden>
        <h3>After autofix · Ruby</h3>
        <p>No autofix was run and no files changed. These pinned versions and advisory examples
          remain unverified; this page cannot report a resolution.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="autofix-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </section>
  </div>
  <script src="../app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
